	<section class="hero alt-hero">
		<div class="hero-badge">Comparison · Self-Hosted Email</div>
		<h1>Stalwart <span>vs</span> Mailcow</h1>
		<p class="alt-lead">
			Two very different answers to the same question. Mailcow assembles the components
			the internet already runs on (Postfix, Dovecot, Rspamd, SOGo) into an 18-service
			Docker stack, with webmail and groupware included. Stalwart rewrites every protocol
			from scratch in one Rust binary, adding JMAP, clustering and pluggable storage on a
			fraction of the RAM, and it's still pre-1.0. Neither ships a transactional sending
			API. If that's the gap, we're a third option, covered below.
		</p>
		<div class="alt-meta" style="margin-top: 1.25rem;">
			<span>Last updated <time datetime={dateModified}>9 October 2026</time></span>
			<span>·</span>
			<span>By the Vectis Mail team</span>
